# PlayMode Test Generation Standards

This file defines mandatory PlayMode test generation standards for Spellwright. PlayMode tests are asynchronous integration tests that validate ECS systems, frame-based behavior, and Unity runtime interactions.

> **Note**: For fast synchronous unit tests of components and queries, see `editmode-tests-generation.mdc`.

## Core Principles

PlayMode tests are:

- **Asynchronous**: Execute across multiple frames using `yield return`
- **Integration-focused**: Test system updates and full ECS workflows
- **Runtime-dependent**: Require Unity's game loop and services
- **Frame-based**: Validate behavior over time
- **Visual-friendly**: Support Gizmos debugging

Use `[UnityTest]` attribute with `IEnumerator` for all PlayMode tests.

## When to Use PlayMode Tests

**Use PlayMode Tests For:**

- System integration across multiple frames
- EntityCommandBuffer system playback
- Time-dependent behavior
- Physics interactions
- Input system integration
- Scene-based testing
- Visual validation with Gizmos

**Example scenarios:**

- "Does the spell move correctly after 3 frames?"
- "Does the homing system acquire and follow targets?"
- "Do systems execute in the correct order?"

## Test Naming Convention

**Format**: `MethodUnderTest_Scenario_ExpectedBehavior`

**Examples:**

```csharp
SpellSpawn_AfterOneFrame_SpellExists()
Movement_AfterThreeFrames_ReachesTarget()
HomingModifier_WithTarget_FollowsTarget()
SystemUpdate_WithECB_ProcessesCommands()
```

## Test Structure

```csharp
using NUnit.Framework;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.TestTools;
using Unity.Entities;
using Unity.Mathematics;
using Unity.Collections;
using System.Collections;

namespace Spellwright.Tests.PlayMode.Systems.Spawning
{
    [TestFixture]
    public class SpellSpawnSystemIntegrationTests
    {
        private World _world;
        private EntityManager _entityManager;
        private InitializationSystemGroup _initGroup;

        [SetUp]
        public void SetUp()
        {
            _world = new World("TestWorld");
            _entityManager = _world.EntityManager;

            _initGroup = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<InitializationSystemGroup>();
            var ecbSystem = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<BeginInitializationEntityCommandBufferSystem>();

            _initGroup.AddSystemToUpdateList(ecbSystem);
            _initGroup.SortSystems();
            _initGroup.Update();
            _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();
        }

        [TearDown]
        public void TearDown()
        {
            if (_world != null && _world.IsCreated)
            {
                _world.Dispose();
            }
        }

        [UnityTest]
        public IEnumerator SpellSpawn_AfterOneFrame_SpellExists()
        {
            Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();
            CreateSpawnRequest(prefab);

            _initGroup.Update();
            _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();

            yield return null;

            var query = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Velocity));
            int spellCount = query.CalculateEntityCount();

            Assert.AreEqual(1, spellCount, "Should spawn one spell after frame");
        }

        private Entity CreateValidPrefab()
        {
            Entity prefab = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Speed { Value = 10f });
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Lifetime { Duration = 5f });
            return prefab;
        }

        private void CreateSpawnRequest(Entity prefab)
        {
            Entity request = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(request, new SpawnRequest
            {
                PrefabEntity = prefab
            });
            _entityManager.AddComponent<ValidatedTag>(request);
        }
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. System Group Management

**Explicit system group setup:**

```csharp
[SetUp]
public void SetUp()
{
    _world = new World("TestWorld");
    _entityManager = _world.EntityManager;

    _initGroup = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<InitializationSystemGroup>();
    var ecbSystem = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<BeginInitializationEntityCommandBufferSystem>();

    _initGroup.AddSystemToUpdateList(ecbSystem);
    _initGroup.SortSystems();
    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();
}
```

### 2. Frame-Based Testing

**Test across multiple frames:**

```csharp
[UnityTest]
public IEnumerator Movement_AfterThreeFrames_ReachesTarget()
{
    Entity spell = CreateMovingSpell();
    float3 startPos = _entityManager.GetComponentData<LocalTransform>(spell).Position;

    yield return null;
    yield return null;
    yield return null;

    float3 endPos = _entityManager.GetComponentData<LocalTransform>(spell).Position;
    float distance = math.distance(startPos, endPos);

    Assert.Greater(distance, 0.1f, "Spell should have moved after 3 frames");
}
```

### 3. Job Completion

**Always complete jobs before assertions:**

```csharp
[UnityTest]
public IEnumerator System_AfterUpdate_ProcessesJobs()
{
    CreateTestData();

    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();

    yield return null;

    int count = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Velocity)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(expectedCount, count);
}
```

### 4. ECB Playback Validation

**Wait for ECB system playback:**

```csharp
[UnityTest]
public IEnumerator ECB_AfterSystemUpdate_EntityCreated()
{
    CreateSpawnRequest();

    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();

    yield return null;

    int spellCount = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Velocity)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(1, spellCount);
}
```

## Visual Testing with Gizmos

**MonoBehaviour for visual debugging:**

```csharp
using Unity.Entities;
using Unity.Mathematics;
using Unity.Collections;
using Unity.Transforms;
using UnityEngine;

namespace Spellwright.Tests.Utilities
{
    public class SpellSpawnVisualizer : MonoBehaviour
    {
        [Header("Visualization Settings")]
        [SerializeField] private bool showVelocityVectors = true;
        [SerializeField] private bool showSpawnPoints = true;
        [SerializeField] private float vectorScale = 1f;
        [SerializeField] private Color velocityColor = Color.cyan;
        [SerializeField] private Color spawnPointColor = Color.yellow;

        private EntityManager _entityManager;
        private EntityQuery _spellQuery;

        private void Start()
        {
            _entityManager = World.DefaultGameObjectInjectionWorld.EntityManager;
            _spellQuery = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(
                typeof(LocalTransform),
                typeof(Velocity)
            );
        }

        private void OnDrawGizmos()
        {
            if (!Application.isPlaying || _entityManager == default) return;
            if (_spellQuery.IsEmpty) return;

            var transforms = _spellQuery.ToComponentDataArray<LocalTransform>(Allocator.Temp);
            var velocities = _spellQuery.ToComponentDataArray<Velocity>(Allocator.Temp);

            for (int i = 0; i < transforms.Length; i++)
            {
                float3 position = transforms[i].Position;
                float3 velocity = velocities[i].Value;

                if (showSpawnPoints)
                {
                    Gizmos.color = spawnPointColor;
                    Gizmos.DrawWireSphere(position, 0.2f);
                }

                if (showVelocityVectors && math.lengthsq(velocity) > 0.001f)
                {
                    Gizmos.color = velocityColor;
                    float3 endPoint = position + math.normalize(velocity) * vectorScale;
                    Gizmos.DrawLine(position, endPoint);
                }
            }

            transforms.Dispose();
            velocities.Dispose();
        }
    }
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

### 1. Don't Use Synchronous Tests

**BAD: No yield, system won't execute properly**

```csharp
[Test]
public void BadFrameTest()
{
    _initGroup.Update();
    int count = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Velocity)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
}
```

**GOOD: Use UnityTest with yield**

```csharp
[UnityTest]
public IEnumerator GoodFrameTest()
{
    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();

    yield return null;

    int count = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Velocity)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
}
```

### 2. Don't Forget Singletons

**BAD: System requires singleton but it doesn't exist**

```csharp
[UnityTest]
public IEnumerator BadSingletonTest()
{
    var system = _world.GetOrCreateSystem<SpellSpawnSystem>();
    _initGroup.Update();
    yield return null;
}
```

**GOOD: Ensure singleton exists in SetUp**

```csharp
[SetUp]
public void SetUp()
{
    _world = new World("TestWorld");
    _entityManager = _world.EntityManager;

    _initGroup = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<InitializationSystemGroup>();
    var ecbSystem = _world.GetOrCreateSystemManaged<BeginInitializationEntityCommandBufferSystem>();

    _initGroup.AddSystemToUpdateList(ecbSystem);
    _initGroup.SortSystems();
    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();
}
```

