## Assertions

### Preferred Assertions for PlayMode

**Frame-based movement:**

```csharp
float3 startPos = GetPosition(entity);
yield return null;
yield return null;
float3 endPos = GetPosition(entity);

float distance = math.distance(startPos, endPos);
Assert.Greater(distance, 0.1f, "Entity should have moved");
```

**Time-dependent values:**

```csharp
Assert.That(actualValue, Is.EqualTo(expectedValue).Within(0.01f));
```

**System execution:**

```csharp
_initGroup.Update();
_entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();
yield return null;

int processedCount = CountProcessedEntities();
Assert.AreEqual(expectedCount, processedCount, "System should process all entities");
```

**Entity state after frames:**

```csharp
yield return new WaitForSeconds(1f);

bool isAlive = _entityManager.Exists(entity);
Assert.IsFalse(isAlive, "Entity should be destroyed after lifetime expires");
```

## Performance Testing

**Benchmarking pattern:**

```csharp
using Unity.PerformanceTesting;

[UnityTest, Performance]
public IEnumerator Spawn_1000Spells_CompletesUnder16ms()
{
    Measure.Frames()
        .WarmupCount(5)
        .MeasurementCount(10)
        .Run();

    for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++)
    {
        CreateSpawnRequest();
    }

    _initGroup.Update();
    _entityManager.CompleteAllTrackedJobs();

    yield return null;
}
```

## Test Maintenance

### PlayMode Test Checklist

- [ ] All tests use `[UnityTest]` with `IEnumerator`
- [ ] All tests `yield return null` at appropriate points
- [ ] Jobs are completed before assertions
- [ ] System groups are properly initialized in SetUp
- [ ] ECB systems are added to system groups
- [ ] World is disposed in TearDown
- [ ] NativeContainers are disposed
- [ ] Test names follow naming convention
- [ ] Clear assertion messages with frame context
- [ ] No hardcoded frame counts (use behavior-based checks)

## Summary

**PlayMode Tests:**

- Asynchronous integration tests with `IEnumerator`
- Test system updates across frames
- Use `yield return null` for frame delays
- Always complete jobs before assertions
- Support visual debugging with Gizmos
- Validate frame-based and time-dependent behavior
- Ensure ECB singletons exist before system updates
